
# 11. Heap Sort

## Question Description
Implement the Heap Sort algorithm in C++ to sort an array in ascending order. Heap Sort uses a binary heap and repeatedly extracts the maximum element to sort the array.

## Test Cases

### Test Case 1
Input: `[12, 11, 13, 5, 6, 7]`

Expected Output:
`[5, 6, 7, 11, 12, 13]`

### Test Case 2
Input: `[4, 10, 3, 5, 1]`

Expected Output:
`[1, 3, 4, 5, 10]`

### Test Case 3
Input: `[9, 8, 7, 6, 5]`

Expected Output:
`[5, 6, 7, 8, 9]`

## Time Complexity
- Best Case: O(n log n)
- Average Case: O(n log n)
- Worst Case: O(n log n)

## Space Complexity
- O(1) auxiliary space for an in-place implementation.
